; 901466-04 Commodore 4040 Disk Drive ROM
;
; The code is Copyright (c) Commodore Business Machines, Inc.
;
; Disassembly and comts are Copyright (c) 2025 Piers Finlayson.
;
; The ROM was sourced from:
; http://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/drives/old/4040/901466-04.bin
;
; 901466-04 is the 4040 disk drive mask programmed 6530 IC, supporting DOS 2.
; The 6530 was mask programmed with the appropriate 1KB ROM image for the
; 4040's secondary processor, the 6504 (a pin reduced 6502).
;
; 901466-01/02 are the 2040/3040 disk drive mask programmed 6530 ICs,
; supporting DOS 1.
;
; As the 2040/3040/4040 are practically identical from a hardware perspective,
; a 2040/3040 can be upgraded by installing the 901466-04 6530 IC and
; replacing the primary processor's ROMs.  This was frequently done.
;
; There may be some very early 2040 units which are do have incompatibilities.
; Raeto West in Programming the PET/CBM states: "Units vary in small details;
; the 2040 board has different ROM slots and is not compatible with the 3040."
; He also states later that "[it] is not particularly easy to upgrade, as its
; internal main printed circuit board has to be changed".  This author (Piers)
; has a 1979 2040, and a DOS 1 3040, and has successfully swapped the ROMs
; between them, so it is unclear what West was referring to.
;
; The key difference between 901466-04 and earlier versions appears to be that
; the job command codes are different.  The 901466-04 requires a job code of
; $D0 to execute arbitrary code, whereas the earlier versions used $60 (ORed
; with 0 or 1 for the drive ID).
